WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.878
(audience cheering)
- All right.

00:00:00.878 --> 00:00:02.113
And in an honor of
Teacher Appreciation Day

00:00:02.113 --> 00:00:05.160
we've invited an audience
full of students and teachers

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:06.610
to hang out with the cast.

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:08.420
That video was of Marianne

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:12.280
who is here with her
teacher, Miss Mulvany.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:15.410
So, was there a teacher who
had a big impact on your lives?

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:16.789
I know we all probably had a teacher that-

00:00:16.789 --> 00:00:17.622
- I must say.

00:00:17.622 --> 00:00:18.709
You're probably still having teachers.

00:00:18.709 --> 00:00:20.077
(all laughing)

00:00:20.077 --> 00:00:22.310
That are really big impacts in your life.

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:23.412
That's so crazy, I'm old.

00:00:23.412 --> 00:00:25.350
(laughing)

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:26.660
So, did you have one?

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.293
- I did, yes. Well many, but,

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.440
Martin Tyrrell was a
fantastic English teacher

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.630
and drama teacher, director of lots

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:35.750
of our shows and just was extraordinary.

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:36.900
I had an amazing art teacher

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:38.240
who said, "You're quite good at art"

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:39.090
and then, you know,

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:40.710
kind of fostered my talent

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:41.740
and made me really believe in it

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:42.910
to the point I got an art scholarship

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:44.772
to the school I was then graduating to.

00:00:44.772 --> 00:00:45.605
- Wow.

00:00:45.605 --> 00:00:46.770
- Having not been good at art at all.

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:49.130
He just saw something
in me and encouraged it

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:51.026
which I think is what great teachers do.

00:00:51.026 --> 00:00:51.859
- Yeah.

00:00:51.859 --> 00:00:53.140
- And they can channel a child's energy

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:55.710
into something productive and something

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:58.020
that gives you security
and a sense of identity

00:00:58.020 --> 00:00:58.990
and belonging
- Confidence.

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:00.410
- and it's wonderful.
- Yeah.

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:01.420
- Teachers are the best.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:03.140
- They see that flicker
and turn it into a flame.

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:04.160
It's like-
- That's right, that is it.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:06.300
- Yeah, I agree. That
happened with me as well.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.140
What about you Benedict W?

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:10.098
(laughing)
- Thank you.

00:01:10.098 --> 00:01:13.250
It was brother Joseph
at Sixth Form College

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:14.140
I used to go to,

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.540
and,

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:17.010
yeah, we were just in English

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:20.700
and it was the "Friends,
Romans, Countrymen" speech

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:23.350
and everyone was passing
it around, reading it

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:25.700
and people were laughing
and it was my turn.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:27.597
I think he stopped the classman,

00:01:27.597 --> 00:01:29.460
"Everybody just pay attention."

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:31.210
I was just like, carried on

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:34.050
and as you say, he sort of

00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:35.420
found the spark really,

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:36.710
that I never knew I had.
- It's empowering.

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:37.703
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:01:37.703 --> 00:01:38.840
- Here I am. (laughing)

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:40.860
- Do you feel like it
changed your personalities?

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:42.110
I feel like it changed mine.

00:01:42.110 --> 00:01:43.990
Like I, once I found like music,

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:46.000
like I love singing and
writing and all that.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.390
It changed my personality.

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:49.350
Do you feel like that happened with y'all?

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:50.183
- Yeah, it's wonderful,

00:01:50.183 --> 00:01:51.016
isn't it?
- Yeah.

00:01:51.016 --> 00:01:52.280
- I mean, just to find the,

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:54.420
just to cultivate as many opportunities

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:56.660
as we can have to see, you know,

00:01:56.660 --> 00:01:57.740
what we can lean into.
- Progress.

00:01:57.740 --> 00:01:58.573
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:01:58.573 --> 00:02:00.080
- Find what resonates with us all and-

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:01.210
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:03.400
- It's exciting and never stop doing that

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:04.233
until you die.
- No.

00:02:04.233 --> 00:02:05.067
- Yeah.
- Mm hm.

00:02:05.067 --> 00:02:06.108
- Well said.
- Yeah.

00:02:06.108 --> 00:02:06.950
- Well said.
- What about you?

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:08.508
So you have a teacher currently.

00:02:08.508 --> 00:02:10.900
Yeah. (laughing)

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:12.260
- Well,

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:13.870
my Wushu teacher,

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:16.220
he's like my coach, Matthew Osborne.

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:19.910
He's been my martial
arts coach since I was 12

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:21.770
and now I'm halfway to my black belt

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:22.861
which is like a really big deal for me.

00:02:22.861 --> 00:02:23.694
- Wow.

00:02:23.694 --> 00:02:25.280
- And that's also very handy
- Yeah.

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:27.080
- for your character probably.
- Yeah.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:28.017
- That's amazing.

00:02:28.017 --> 00:02:30.250
(audience applauding)
- And then, you know,

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:32.470
he's very kind of tough on me, you know,

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:36.570
keeps me patient and, you know, humble,

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:40.240
but he's very charismatic
and funny and, you know,

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:41.520
that's what makes him such a good teacher.

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:43.670
It makes me like want to do better

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:47.130
and actually, you know, continue,

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:47.963
cuz if I didn't, I mean,

00:02:47.963 --> 00:02:51.553
he would let me know.
(laughing)

